// Level 4: The Hospital Wing (working name), the hardest: a hospital's two three-storey wings in an L round an overgrown
// courtyard. World frame: metres, x east, z south (north is −Z), y up. A fence encloses x −55…55, z −40…40; you come in
// at the gate in the south side, the breach in the east side or the hole in the west side.
// The north wing (x −48…8, z −36…−22) and the west wing (x −48…−34, z −22…18) meet at the corner stairs; the courtyard
// fills the L (x −34…8, z −22…18); the north wing's east end has fallen in. Outside: the ambulance bay under its canopy
// (east), the boiler house and its chimney (north-east), the car park (south) and the gatehouse by the gate.
// Fence segments: 0 north (x −55→55, at_m = x + 55), 1 east (z −40→40, at_m = z + 40),
// 2 south (x 55→−55, at_m = 55 − x), 3 west (z 40→−40, at_m = 40 − z).
// The north wing's local frame is world + (48, 0, 36), the west wing's world + (48, 0, 22). Floors are 3.4 m apart.
